%% @fig 01
%% @kicker What fills the window
%% @alt A fixed-size context window is filled by four inputs: the system prompt, the conversation history, retrieved documents, and the agent's scratchpad. Whatever capacity is left is the headroom for the model's next response and tool calls. When it overflows, naive truncation cuts the oldest messages first.
%% @caption The context window is a fixed buffer, and short-term memory is whatever it holds during one run.
